sections.body_md:
All capital losses (discount or loss on issue of debentures) are written off **in the year in which they occur**. The sequence is:
1. **Securities Premium** (permitted by Section 52 of the Companies Act, 2013; premium received on any issue, including one in the same year);
2. **Statement of Profit and Loss**;
3. lastly **Capital Reserve**.

Entry: Securities Premium A/c Dr., Statement of Profit and Loss Dr., Capital Reserve A/c Dr. To Discount (or Loss) on Issue of Debentures A/c.

questions.stem_md:
Mount Harriet Spice Mills Ltd, an imagined company at Port Blair, receives in full the application money on three issues of 1,000 debentures of ₹100 each, payable in one sum. Pass the allotment entries for:

(a) 8% debentures issued at a discount of 5% and redeemable at par;
(b) 9% debentures issued at a premium of 8% and redeemable at a premium of 5%;
(c) 10% debentures issued at a discount of 4% and redeemable at a premium of 6%.
